      "text": "Let's denote the determinant of matrix $\\mathbf{M}$ by $| \\mathbf{M} |$. Then, we have $| \\mathbf{M} | = -2$.\n\nWe want to find $| \\mathbf{M} |^4$, which is the determinant of $\\mathbf{M}^4$. Since matrix multiplication is associative, we have:\n\n$$| \\mathbf{M} |^4 = | \\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M} | = | \\mathbf{M}^4 |$$\n$$| \\mathbf{M}^4 | = | \\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M} | = (\\det (\\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M}) \\cdot \\det (\\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M}))$$\n$$\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (\\det (\\mathbf{M}^2) \\cdot \\det (\\mathbf{M}))$$\n\nNote that $| \\mathbf{M}^2 | = (\\det (\\mathbf{M} \\cdot \\mathbf{M}))$, so we have:\n\n$$\\det (\\mathbf{M}^4) = (\\det (\\mathbf{M}^2) \\cdot \\det (\\mathbf{M})) = (| \\mathbf{M} |^2 \\cdot | \\mathbf{M} |) = (-2)^2 \\cdot (-2) = 4 \\cdot (-2) = \\boxed{-8}$$",
